    "body": "## Problem\r\n'equalalways' is not applied when Neovim is resized, making windows uneven.\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\nEqualize windows on VimResized autocmd when 'equalalways' is set, respecting the 'eadirection' setting. Add functional tests for the supported option values too.\r\n\r\nAI-assisted\r\n\r\nCloses #41059 ",
    "closed_at": "2026-09-21T16:17:04Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Use of 'eadirection' is a good idea, https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/41396 was missing that.\r\n\r\n123 lines of test code is excessive, there is not much reason to add tests for a trivial default. And the tests look like they could be minimized anyway, which is always a requirement for PRs. Please review https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md#ai-assisted-work",
